        "structured_payload": null,
        "subject_scope": {
          "template_id": "arkham_asylum_cell_intake"
        },
        "temporal_scope": {},
        "text": "A sealed women's ward isolation cell (two cots, shared head, a reinforced door, and a high observation aperture) makes first contact intimate before the larger system commits: whoever already reads the room sets tempo for cohabitation, and noise from the corridor is a reminder that power can re-enter at any moment. Intake is lived here; informal hierarchy and fear of the next move (rounds, shower blocks, the mess) shape what gets said and what is deferred until staff, a ward peer enforcer, or a credentialed officer steps into view.",
        "visibility": "template_participants"
