          "template_id": "arkham_asylum_mess_hall_arena"
        },
        "temporal_scope": {},
        "text": "A line-served women's ward mess hall is a low-privacy, high-visibility room: long tables, plastic chairs, and worn murals under hard lighting force parallel attention to food, pecking order, and staff sightlines. Predatory talk, a sudden impulse grab, or a pairwise blow-up at a table can all escalate in full view; guards and uniformed response sit at the room's margin with proximity but not always instant reach, so the beat can fork between coordinated table pressure, an opportunistic disruption that re-routes authority, and dyadic public volatility before the room is reset.",
        "visibility": "template_participants"
